  "body_text": "Monitor biodiversity using environmental DNA (eDNA)\nEnvironmental DNA (eDNA) \n        Environmental DNA (eDNA) enables the detection and identification of species present in an ecosystem from water, soil, sediment, or biofilm samples.LDgenX provides tailored eDNA solutions to support biodiversity monitoring, conservation, and environmental impact assessments.\n            Approches\n        Metabarcoding\nBiodiversity assessment using targeted genetic markers (e.g. 12S, COI, 18S, ITS).Metagenomics\nComprehensive analysis of biological communities through untargeted sequencing.\n Targeted dPCR\nUltra-sensitive detection and quantification of target species or pathogens using digital PCR (dPCR).\n Long-Read Sequencing\nEnhanced taxonomic resolution and expanded analytical capabilities through long-read sequencing technologies.\n            Services\n        12345678910\n            Case study\n        Ichthyological Survey for the Artois–Picardie Water Agency\n                Read more\n            Detection and monitoring of fish communities in turbid waters using environmental DNA (eDNA)Baseline Marine Biodiversity Assessment at a Pilot Site\n        Biodiversity Monitoring of Offshore Wind Farms\n\nLet’s discuss your project\n        \n        Do you wish to implement biodiversity monitoring, study a population, or develop a specific molecular tool ?\n    \n                Contact our team",
  "metadata_path": "source/en/services__environmental-dna-edna.json"
